							<div align="center"><font color="#000000"><b><u><br /><font color="#ffffff" size="4"><img src="/pics/2103/raidexplanation.jpg" /><br /><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3">Raiding and The DKP System</font></font></u></b></font><br /> <div align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3">Alright ladies and gentlemen, this page is going to be dedicated entirely to the system that Soldier will be using on Raids. The first thing I would like to do is to discuss what exactly constitutes a Raid. <br /></font> <div align="center"><img src="/pics/2103/drake.jpg" /><font color="#000000"> </font><br /></div><font color="#d3d3d3"><font face="Verdana"><font size="4"><u><b>The Raid</b></u></font><br />A Raid is a scheduled event with a specific goal in mind. A good example of this would be, "Raid on Onyxia, Goal: To clear to Onyxia and attempt to kill the dragon."&nbsp; <br />The Raid will have a scheduled time with it. In this raid mentioned above the guild will gather together and form a <u>Raid Party</u>. The raid party is composed of&nbsp; <b>at least</b> two groups of players. <br /><br />After gathering for the raid there will be a period in which the Raid Party kills mobs in between the beginning of the zone to the desired target, this is called&nbsp; <b>clearing</b>. <br />During the clearing period on a Raid, any loot that drops, will be based on a need/use basis. Where if you need something and will use it you can enter the random roll for the loot that drops. <br /><br />After the clearing is finished and the desired <b>mob</b>(monster) is ready to be engaged there will be a necessary rebuff and preparation period. This is why the clearing is done so we can rest for a few moments in preparation for the target mob we are going after. In this case it would be our goal to engage Onyxia and make notes of how the encounter is.<br />&nbsp;<br /><font size="4"><b><u>DKP System</u></b></font><br />Though if the purpose of the is to kill a targeted mob and there is loot that drops it will be awarded based on the DKP system in use on all of our raids. Though first, a little background on the DKP system. <br /><br />The DKP system, is short for Dragon Kill Points system. In this system points are awarded to a member for attending every raid. Every raid has a specific point value. A person must be present for the entirety of a raid to get full DKP points awarded to them.&nbsp; An example of this would be the raid mentioned above. If a player was present for the entire Raid, the clearing period and the engagement of Onyxia, the player would be awarded a number of points. <br /><br />The points in turn are stored and kept track of online at our website. These points earned can be used to bid on items that drop off target monsters on Raids. These items will also have a number of DKP attatched to them. <br /><br /><font size="4"><b><u>Winning an Item</u></b></font><br />If a person wins an item on a Raid that number of DKP will be deducted from their total number. A player may win an item that is worth more DKP than they have.&nbsp; This will obviously put them into a negative situation of DKP and may not bid on another item until their DKP is positive once again. <br /><br />There is a priority system when an item drops off a targeted mob. If player A has 25 DKP and bids on a 12dkp item, and player B has 40 DKP and bids on the same item; player B will win it due to them having more DKP earned overall. This encourages everyone to go on Raids frequently to earn more DKP and get better equipment, not only to help themselves but the guild as well.&nbsp; <br /><br />Thanks and good luck, <br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </font></font><font color="#0000ff"><font face="Verdana"><font size="4">The Soldier Staff </font><br /></font></font></div></div>
							
